## Chapter 11: Full Exam Simulation and Scoring Strategy — Flashcards

| # | Front (Question) | Back (Answer) |
|---|-----------------|---------------|
| 1 | CCAR-P exam structure: number of questions and time limit? | 63 questions in 120 minutes. Exam tip: budget ~114 seconds (1 min 54 sec) per question. |
| 2 | CCAR-P scaled score range and passing threshold? | Scale is 100-1000; passing threshold is 700. Exam tip: 700 is NOT 70% raw score — it reflects psychometric scaling, not raw percentage. |
| 3 | Average time budget per question on the CCAR-P exam? | ~114 seconds (1 min 54 sec). Exam tip: check pace at Q16 (~30 min elapsed), Q32 (~60 min), Q48 (~90 min). |
| 4 | Visual cue for a multiple-response question in OnVUE? | Square checkboxes instead of round radio buttons. Exam tip: the question text always states the exact number of options to select. |
| 5 | Partial credit rule for multiple-response questions? | None — scoring is all-or-nothing on the exact correct set. Exam tip: selecting 1 of 2 correct answers still scores zero. |
| 6 | Best flagging strategy for a timed, single-pass exam? | Flag only uncertain questions, submit a best-guess answer first, then revisit flagged items with remaining time. Exam tip: never leave a flagged question unanswered in case time expires. |
| 7 | Domain-weighted review priority rule? | Review flagged questions from higher-weighted domains first. Exam tip: an error in a 30%-weighted domain costs more scaled points than one in a 10%-weighted domain. |
| 8 | OnVUE pre-exam room requirement? | 360-degree webcam room scan with a clear desk, no secondary monitors, and no printed materials. Exam tip: failing the scan can delay or cancel the session. |
| 9 | Microphone requirement during OnVUE proctored exam? | Must remain active for the entire session for continuous proctor audio monitoring. |
| 10 | Scaled score vs raw percentage — key difference? | Scaled score normalizes for item difficulty across different exam forms; it is NOT a direct raw percentage of correct answers. |
| 11 | Pacing checkpoint rule for 63-question / 120-minute exam? | By question 32 (just past halfway), ~60 minutes should be elapsed. Exam tip: more than 5 minutes behind at this checkpoint means switch to skip-and-flag mode. |
| 12 | What to do with leftover time after answering all 63 questions? | Review flagged questions in order of domain weight, highest-weighted first. Exam tip: never leave an item unanswered — unanswered counts the same as wrong. |
